    <content type="html">&lt;a href=&#34;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12465978/can-aws-security-groups-on-one-aws-account-reference-security-groups-in-another&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img&#xA;        src=&#34;https://shots.wayl.one/shot/?url=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12465978/can-aws-security-groups-on-one-aws-account-reference-security-groups-in-another&amp;height=450&amp;width=800&amp;scaled_width=800&amp;scaled_height=450&amp;selectors=&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;shot of post - Cross Account AWS Security Group ID Reference&#34;&#xA;        height=450&#xA;        width=800&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s my thought on &lt;a href=&#34;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12465978/can-aws-security-groups-on-one-aws-account-reference-security-groups-in-another&#34;&gt;Cross Account AWS Security Group ID Reference&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I needed to update some ingress rules across several AWS accounts and ran into an issue when I had to reference a security group id in another account - turns out &lt;accountid&gt;/&lt;securitygroupid&gt; is the money maker&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;EDIT: this requires VPC Peering&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;admonition note&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;admonition-title&#34;&gt;Note&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is one of [[ my-thoughts ]]. I picked this up from &lt;a href=&#34;https://waylonwalker.com&#34;&gt;Waylon Walker&lt;/a&gt;(&lt;a href=&#34;https://thoughts.waylonwalker.com&#34;&gt;https://thoughts.waylonwalker.com&lt;/a&gt;). It&amp;rsquo;s a short note that I make about someone else&amp;rsquo;s content online.  Learn more about the process &lt;a href=&#34;/thoughts/&#34; class=&#34;wikilink&#34; data-title=&#34;Thoughts&#34; data-description=&#34;My thoughts are found at my thoughts feed&#34; data-date=&#34;2025-06-09&#34; data-preview=&#34;My thoughts are found at my thoughts feed&#34;&gt;Thoughts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#x